    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0637" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/10–2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d524-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-20T00:00:00-04:00">October 20,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8717. Department’s 8015, September 30<anchor n="29" xml:id="d524-f2"/> and 8208,
                    October 7. British made formal protest Saturday<anchor n="30" xml:id="d524-f3"/>
                    to our direct transmission to Russians of our reply to Sir Ronald Campbell’s
                    letters on European Economic Commission. For your information only transmission
                    was to avoid in appearance or in fact a joint presentation to Russians of a plan
                    previously agreed between US and UK.</p>
                <p>British and Department are considering because of urgency that if Russians are
                    likely to delay their reply, for any considerable period, we might commence
                    joint US–UK discussions in London with a Russian observer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d524-f1" n="28" type="source" xml:id="d524-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Moscow as telegram 2482, for information only.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d524-f2" n="29" xml:id="d524-f2-content">
